WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.520
Sabine, Ezra, Grand Admiral Thrawn: The latest&nbsp;
episode of Ahsoka revolves around some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:09.420
franchise's most popular characters —&nbsp;
and that's not necessarily a good thing.

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:16.680
"A long time ago, in a galaxy far, far away…"

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:23.220
Ahsoka's sixth episode is arguably the most&nbsp;
exciting installment in the series yet. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:27.300
adventure introduces a brand-new galaxy, a&nbsp;
bewitching planet with a mysterious backstory,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.660
a few cutesy creatures that will&nbsp;
no doubt boost merch sales, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:34.380
of course, Grand Admiral Thrawn himself.&nbsp;
And that's not to mention the long-awaited&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:38.100
reunion between Sabine Wren and Ezra&nbsp;
Bridger. However, this episode also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.400
typifies one of the biggest problems with&nbsp;
the Star Wars franchise in recent years.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.620
Namely: Ahsoka Tano is relegated to the&nbsp;
sidelines in Episode 6. She and Huyang&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.680
receive a courtesy scene at the beginning&nbsp;
of the episode, but the rest of the story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:53.820
is dedicated to Sabine's quest to find Ezra.&nbsp;
There's no denying that Sabine has always been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:57.060
determined to find her friend, but it's&nbsp;
been Ahsoka's mission for a long time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:01.500
too. Episode 6 robs her of her goal&nbsp;
— and in her own series, no less.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.640
This isn't the first time that a Disney+&nbsp;
Star Wars series has made the main character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.900
a sidekick in their own show. In fact, this&nbsp;
is becoming something of a recurring issue.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.860
The Book of Boba Fett rubbed Star Wars&nbsp;
fans the wrong way in a number of ways.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:17.940
The slow pacing, frequent repetition, and poor&nbsp;
character development are just some of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:22.260
criticisms that have been lobbied at the bounty&nbsp;
hunter's spin-off series. However, arguably the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:26.460
biggest sin was making him a side character in no&nbsp;
fewer than two episodes of his own solo project.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:30.480
Chapter 5 and Chapter 6 of The Book of&nbsp;
Boba Fett both see Boba take a backseat&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.560
to Din Djarin and Grogu; they're pretty much&nbsp;
the two best episodes in the entire series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.940
too. It's here that Grogu receives his&nbsp;
Jedi training courtesy of Luke Skywalker,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:43.080
which is more significant to the greater narrative&nbsp;
than anything that happens in Boba's own journey.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:47.040
But here's the thing: Din and Grogu&nbsp;
already have their own series. Giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.160
them such a prominent presence in The&nbsp;
Book of Boba Fett took a lot of shine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.820
off a character who has been a fan favorite&nbsp;
since The Empire Strikes Back. Basically,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:57.240
his first solo outing will go down in&nbsp;
history as a missed opportunity to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:00.960
him the focus he deserved, as well as the&nbsp;
series fans always wanted. Then again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.980
the characters who overshadowed him were actually&nbsp;
subjected to the same treatment in their own show.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:06.720
"This is the way."

00:02:07.380 --> 00:02:08.580
"This is the way."

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:10.500
"This is the way."

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.820
The Mandalorian started out as&nbsp;
a story about a wandering bounty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:18.840
hunter. Din Djarin eventually takes on the&nbsp;
role of protector to the adorable Grogu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:22.140
and their relationship quickly becomes&nbsp;
the focus of the show. Unfortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:26.340
in Season 3, the main players get lost in the&nbsp;
shuffle as other characters take precedence.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.800
The Book of Boba Fett is partly to blame for this.&nbsp;
The titular bounty hunter's series reunites Din&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.400
and his little green sidekick after they were&nbsp;
separated in The Mandalorian's second season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:39.660
and the resolution robs their own series of&nbsp;
an engaging storyline with stakes and drama.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:43.620
The end result? Bo-Katan Kryze, of all&nbsp;
people, turns out to be the main character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:47.940
in The Mandalorian Season 3. The show's&nbsp;
meatiest storyline chronicles her journey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:51.000
to reunite the people of Mandalore —&nbsp;
which is an interesting arc for her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:53.220
but not for the characters this&nbsp;
show is supposed to be about.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:57.240
Meanwhile, Din's quest for redemption among&nbsp;
his people is resolved in just a few episodes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.240 --> 00:03:01.560
undermining his entire journey until&nbsp;
that point. It's clumsy storytelling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.280
and it's understandable why there are concerns&nbsp;
about Ahsoka experiencing similar issues.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:08.520
It remains to be seen how the rest of&nbsp;
Ahsoka's first season will play out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:12.180
but the current signs suggest a danger&nbsp;
of her becoming the latest victim of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:16.740
franchise's sidekick trend. Sabine's journey&nbsp;
has arguably been the most interesting so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:20.400
and Episode 6 positions her as the&nbsp;
potential star of the show moving forward.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:24.720
Additionally, with a fan-favorite character like&nbsp;
Ezra back on the board, the upcoming episodes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:29.400
will undoubtedly be dedicated to continuing his&nbsp;
story as well. But will that also come at the cost&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:34.740
of Ahsoka being given less to do? Episode 6 does&nbsp;
tease a future showdown between Ahsoka and Thrawn,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:38.640
though it's likely that Ezra will also factor&nbsp;
into the final battle with the Grand Admiral

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:42.120
At this point, it's probably fair to&nbsp;
say that most of the Disney+ shows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:46.380
exist to contribute to a larger overarching&nbsp;
story with many moving parts. That's fine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.380 --> 00:03:49.020
of course — but many fans will no&nbsp;
doubt hope that they're able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.840
make these protagonists feel more&nbsp;
integral to their own adventures.

